Translation patch: the OAuth metadata URL and issuer checks of
crates/rmcp/src/transport/auth.rs, so that targets A04-A10 translate (A04 is_http_url, A05
is_disallowed_metadata_host, A06 is_allowed_metadata_url, A07 resolve_resource_metadata_url, A08
validate_authorization_response_issuer, A09 validate_authorization_metadata_issuer, A10
validate_resource_metadata_resource; human decisions 2026-11-26 and 2026-11-27, recorded as
AD1-AD8 in formal/README.md: AD1 patch 06 with the mirror enum IssuerError, the check_* helpers as the
verified targets of A08-A10 and the validate_* wrappers as unverified glue, A04 linkage
patch-06; AD2 the tracing events keep the target rmcp::transport::auth; AD3
#[allow(clippy::nonminimal_bool)] on the three functions that use `!(a == b)`; AD4 the opaque
constants of the external models and the exact model of trim; AD5 the boundary tests of these
targets go into 02-phase2-tests.patch, not into this patch; AD6
#[allow(clippy::enum_variant_names)] on IssuerError; AD7 and AD8 two of the three stated
exceptions below)

Applies to: the copy of upstream origin/main 7caec762799bece6fba38e4298b8ca7db8bac12c after
01-request-state-wire.patch, 02-phase2-tests.patch, 03-request-state-public.patch,
04-skill-public.patch and 05-metadata-resolver.patch (scripts/apply-patches.sh applies
formal/trusted/patches/*.patch in file-name order, patch -p1 -F 0, only to the copy in
