(blob 3d7816b upstream, 83bcae7 after patches 02 and 05, dad471b after this patch). Generated
with git diff from the patch-01..05 copy. The patch body below is the authoritative content. Toolchain measured: Aeneas
nightly-2026.11.24-fb44cb4, Charon 0.1.324, Rust nightly-2026-09-17.

Not part of this patch (they stay in the repository): the Charon settings in
crates/rmcp/Cargo.toml (seven start_from entries rmcp::transport::auth::_::{is_http_url,
is_disallowed_metadata_host, is_allowed_metadata_url, resolve_resource_metadata_url,
check_authorization_response_issuer, check_authorization_metadata_issuer,
check_resource_metadata_resource}; the opaque entry rmcp::transport::auth::prim), TARGETS and
PATCH06_TARGETS of scripts/aeneas-translate.sh, the patch06 set of
scripts/check-original-linkage.sh, the translation pin, and the external models of
formal/trusted/Rmcp/FunsExternal.lean (section "auth.rs OAuth metadata URL and issuer checks").
All seven targets and their helpers need this patch (linkage patch-06): A04 translates
unmodified but its Lean does not build (H3); is_same_origin translates unmodified and is reached
only from A07.

Stays unverified (not translated, or translated only as an opaque model): the wrappers
validate_authorization_response_issuer, validate_authorization_metadata_issuer (which reads
self.allow_missing_issuer) and validate_resource_metadata_resource (which reads self.base_url),
and IssuerError::into_auth_error (H6, H10); the bodies of the ten prim functions (opaque, modelled
in Lean); URL parsing, resolution and rewriting (url::Url::parse, join and the setters behind
prim::issuer_url: opaque values of the opaque type url::Url, no axiom).
Stated exceptions (the same three in the header of patch 06, the section docstring of
FunsExternal.lean and the module docstring of Proofs.External.Auth): (1) AD7: the `issuer_url`
setters can panic for a discovery URL longer than `u32::MAX` bytes; the model returns `ok`. (2) AD8:
the `debug_assert!` of `Url::join` (url-2.5.9 `src/parser.rs` line 1304) can panic for a `file:`
base whose last path segment is a normalized Windows drive letter; the model returns `ok`. (3)
The `tracing` side effect of the four log functions is not modelled; they return `()`. Details:
 AD7  model of prim::issuer_url: for a discovery URL with neither query nor fragment whose
      serialization is longer than u32::MAX bytes (which Url::parse and Url::join accept, since
      they check only the start offsets of the components), set_path panics at
      `to_u32(self.serialization.len()).unwrap()` (url-2.5.9 src/lib.rs line 1768); the model
      returns `ok`; A09 statements take a premise bounding the URL
      (formal/trusted/Rmcp/FunsExternal.lean, transport.auth.prim.issuer_url).
 AD8  model of url::Url::join (decision 2026-11-27): with debug assertions on (the translated
      configuration), for a file: base whose last path segment is a normalized Windows drive
      letter (pop_path does not pop it) joined with a leading `..` or percent-encoded double-dot
      segment, Url::join can panic at
      `debug_assert!(self.serialization.as_bytes()[segment_start - 1] == b'/')` (url-2.5.9
      src/parser.rs line 1304), e.g. Url::parse("file://h/x/C:").unwrap().join("..")
      (reproduced 2026-11-27; a reviewer's fuzzing found 595 such panics, all file: bases, all at
      line 1304, none for other schemes; the condition is a superset description:
      Url::parse("file:///C:").unwrap().join("..") does not panic); the model returns `ok`; A07 statements assume the
      base URL's scheme is http or https (formal/trusted/Rmcp/FunsExternal.lean, url.Url.join).

Change (non-test lines only; no test is added or changed). Every hunk replaces code that the
translation cannot handle by calls to the new module `prim`, by a helper function or by an
explicit match, and keeps the computed values:
 prim  New private module `prim` at the end of auth.rs (before `mod tests`), opaque in the
       translation and modelled in Lean, each the original expression: trim (`s.trim()`),
       starts_with (`s.starts_with(prefix)`), strip_suffix (`s.strip_suffix(suffix)`, &str
       pattern), strip_dir_prefix (`path.strip_prefix(&format!("{prefix}/"))`),
       trim_start_slashes (`s.trim_start_matches('/')`), issuer_url (the original
       clone/set_query/set_fragment/set_path/to_string lines of
       expected_issuer_for_authorization_metadata_url, verbatim), and the four tracing events
       of resolve_resource_metadata_url (debug!/warn! with the original messages and
       `target: "rmcp::transport::auth"`, AD2). Used by H5, H7 and H10.
 H1  The constant CLOUD_METADATA_HOSTS (a `&[&str]`) is removed and its one use,
     `CLOUD_METADATA_HOSTS.contains(&host)` in is_disallowed_metadata_hostname, becomes
     `matches!(host, "metadata" | "metadata.google.internal" | "metadata.azure.internal")`.
 H2  A05 is_disallowed_metadata_hostname / is_disallowed_metadata_host:
     `metadata_resolver::prim::ends_with(host, ".localhost")` and
     `metadata_resolver::prim::trim_end_dots(domain)` for `host.ends_with(".localhost")` and
     `domain.trim_end_matches('.')` (the patch-05 wrappers).
 H3  A04 is_http_url, A06 is_allowed_metadata_url: the parameter `url` is renamed `target`; A07
     resolve_resource_metadata_url: the local `url` is renamed `metadata_url` (and the closure
     argument of is_root_url, H8, is `parsed`).
 H4  A06 is_allowed_metadata_url: `Self::is_disallowed_metadata_host(host)` without
     `host.clone()` (Host<&str> is Copy); the rest of the body moves to the new private
     `is_allowed_disallowed_host(base_url, host, allow_private)`, called with the host read
     again by `match target.host() { Some(host) => .., None => false }` (a comment in the code
     says that the `None` arm is unreachable, the host having been `Some` just above, and is
     there only to make the match total); there
     `IpAddr::V4(addr)`/`IpAddr::V6(addr)` for `addr.into()`, and the closure
     `|base_host| Self::is_loopback_metadata_host(base_host)` for the fn item in `is_some_and`.
 H5  A07 resolve_resource_metadata_url: `prim::trim(value)` for `value.trim()`;
     `Url::parse(value).or_else(|_| base_url.join(value))` becomes a nested match; the four
     debug!/warn! calls become the prim functions; `url.scheme() != "https"` becomes
     `!(metadata_url.scheme() == "https")` (H9).
 H6  A08/A09: the bodies of validate_authorization_response_issuer and
     validate_authorization_metadata_issuer move to the new private
     check_authorization_response_issuer(stored_state, received_issuer) and
     check_authorization_metadata_issuer(allow_missing_issuer, discovery_url, expected_issuer,
     metadata), which return the new private enum IssuerError (variants AuthorizationFailed,
     AuthorizationServerMissingIssuer, AuthorizationServerMismatch, with the names and fields
     of the AuthError variants they stand for); each validate_* is
     `Self::check_*(..).map_err(IssuerError::into_auth_error)`, passing
     `self.allow_missing_issuer` for A09. In check_authorization_metadata_issuer
     `expected_issuer.map(str::to_owned).or_else(|| ..)` becomes a match.
 H7  expected_issuer_for_authorization_metadata_url (A09 callee):
     `prim::strip_dir_prefix(path, oauth_prefix)` (and for oidc_prefix) for
     `path.strip_prefix(&format!("{prefix}/"))`, `prim::strip_suffix` and
