Why each hunk is needed (measured 2026-11-26 in a scratch copy with the Charon settings and
scripts above; each error is what Aeneas, Charon or the Lean build reports without the hunk):
 prim, H5, H7, H10  "[Error] Unimplemented" on the signatures of str::trim, starts_with,
     strip_prefix, strip_suffix, trim_start_matches, ends_with (the core::str::pattern::Pattern
     trait has a generic associated type, as patches 04 and 05); the tracing macros expand to
     callsite statics ("Mixed declaration groups" and internal errors); `format!` and the url
     setters would need models of alloc::fmt::format, core::fmt::Arguments and the url parser.
 H1  "[Error] Unimplemented" at every use of a constant of type &[&str] or [&str; N]; a local
     array translates but needs a model of slice::contains.
 H2  The Pattern error of prim.
 H3  Not a translation error: the Lean build fails ("Invalid field `Url`: the environment does
     not contain `url.Url.Url`"), since Aeneas emits `url.Url.scheme url` with a local variable
     named `url` that shadows the namespace (as patch 05 H7). Remove H3 when Aeneas qualifies
     the name.
 H4  `Host<&str>::clone` gives "Found a case of unsupported nested borrows"; a `match` on a host
     bound by let-else that binds its fields gives "[Error] Internal error" (interp/Interp.ml
     line 686); `addr.into()` gives an internal error; `is_some_and` with the fn item gives
     "[Error] Unimplemented" (the FnOnce impl of a fn item with a higher-ranked lifetime, as
     patch 05).
 H5  `or_else` with a closure: the same fn-item/closure limitation; see also prim.
 H6  AuthError cannot be translated: "Dynamic trait types are not supported yet" on the field
     `source: Box<dyn Error + Send + Sync>` of AuthError::DiscoveryRequestFailed, and with
     AuthError opaque Aeneas fails "Can't get the list of fields of this adt" at the variant
     constructors. Reading a field of `&self` (the opaque AuthorizationManager, human decision
     H4) gives "Unexpected error". `.map(str::to_owned)`: "Unimplemented" (fn item as closure).
 H8  The closure with `filter`/`map`/`unwrap_or` gives "Nested borrows are not supported yet".
 H9  `str::to_string` goes through the blanket alloc::string::ToString over Display/Formatter,
     which has no exact model (`str::to_owned` has one). With `!=` Aeneas adds the default
     method `ne` to every PartialEq instance record of the crate, which changes the blocks of
     ORIGINAL items (such as the instance of NumberOrString) that
     scripts/check-original-linkage.sh compares. AD3: without the allow, cargo clippy reports five
     clippy::nonminimal_bool warnings on these expressions.
 H10 "Unexpected error" on the field access `self.base_url` of the opaque AuthorizationManager.
No upstream Charon or Aeneas issue has been filed (as of 2026-11-26); the reproducers are kept
outside the repository.

Why the behaviour is unchanged: every value computed is the same and in the same order. The
prim functions are the original expressions with the same arguments; a char pattern '/' and the
&str pattern "/" match the same single byte; `matches!` on the three literals is
`CLOUD_METADATA_HOSTS.contains`; Url::host is a pure accessor, so reading it again yields the
host that was cloned; `IpAddr::V4(a)` is `<IpAddr as From<Ipv4Addr>>::from(a)`; the closures
call the functions the fn items named; the nested match tries Url::parse first and joins only on
its error, as or_else; `!(a == b)` is the default `ne`; str::to_string and str::to_owned both
return String::from(s); IssuerError::into_auth_error maps each variant to the AuthError variant
of the same name with the same fields, so each validate_* returns what its old body returned;
the fields self.allow_missing_issuer and self.base_url are read once, before the body, and
nothing in the body changes them; trim_root_slash returns `without_slash` exactly when the old
filter kept it. The tracing events keep their level, message and target
(`target: "rmcp::transport::auth"`, the module path the macros used before, AD2); only their
callsite metadata (module_path rmcp::transport::auth::prim, file line) differs, which no target
or level filter reads.
Warnings: the property that matters is that patch 06 adds no warning: cargo clippy -p rmcp --lib
--no-default-features --features request-state,server,client,client-side-sse,
transport-streamable-http-server,transport-streamable-http-client,auth (the translated feature
configuration), with and without the feature macros, reports the same set of warnings (same
lint, file and message; only the line numbers in auth.rs move) on the patch-01..05 copy and on
the patch-01..06 copy, and none of them is clippy::nonminimal_bool or
clippy::enum_variant_names (measured 2026-11-26). The totals depend on the toolchain, not on
macros: 10 with the repository toolchain 1.96 (clippy 0.1.96: nine dead-code warnings and the
patch-05 redundant_closure), 29 with the pinned nightly-2026-09-17 (the same ten plus 18
clippy::result_large_err and one clippy::question_mark, the last on the `else if let ... else
{ return None; }` chain of expected_issuer_for_authorization_metadata_url, which H7 keeps), each
on both copies and with or without macros. Two lints are allowed on items this patch adds:
AD3 #[allow(clippy::nonminimal_bool)] (above, H9); AD6 #[allow(clippy::enum_variant_names)] on
IssuerError, whose three variants all begin with `Authorization` because they copy the names of
the AuthError variants they stand for exactly (AuthorizationFailed,
AuthorizationServerMissingIssuer, AuthorizationServerMismatch), so that into_auth_error maps
each variant to the one of the same name; without the allow clippy reports "all variants have
the same prefix: `Authorization`". The crate does not deny warnings.
Tests: cargo test --lib (features request-state, server, client, client-side-sse,
transport-streamable-http-server, transport-streamable-http-client, auth, macros) on the patched
copy: 860 passed, 0 failed, among them the thirteen AD5 boundary tests d5_* of patch 02 (counts in
formal/trusted/evidence/README.md).

